<span id="A2.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt Instruction</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T8.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">You are a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) model. Your task is to carry out multiple iterative processes, continuously decompose a problem into sub-problems, solve them one by one, and finally answer the original question.
We will provide you with a question and the previous iteration history (each iteration includes the thinking process, sub-question, the model’s answers to the sub-questions based on its own knowledge or the relevant documents retrieved from the sub-question). Please continue reasoning along the previous iteration history to solve the original problem.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T8.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">After reasoning, if you find you lack some knowledge, you can call a search engine by &lt;search&gt; query &lt;/search&gt;, and it will return the top searched results between &lt;information&gt; and &lt;/information&gt;. If you find that no further external knowledge is needed, please still provide your reasoning process, and then you can directly provide the answers within &lt;answer&gt; and &lt;/answer&gt;. For example, &lt;answer&gt; Beijing &lt;/answer&gt;.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T8.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">*Ensure both queries and answers are concise, using nouns or short phrases whenever possible.**</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T8.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Matters Need Attention:</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T8.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">*1. Please note that the previous iteration history is true and does not need to be verified again, so you can definitely take this information as established facts and, based on this, continue to reason downward.**</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T8.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:398.3pt;">
<span id="A2.T8.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">*2. Please note that during the reasoning process, do not end it casually. Only when you think it necessary to call the search engine (the output ends with &lt;/search&gt;) or output the final answer (the output ends with &lt;/answer&gt;) can the reasoning process be temporarily interrupted or completely ended.**</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T8.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T8.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
